We apply the following patches to upstream source code.

libtommath/bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c:

1) Guard platform-specific calls in s_mp_rand_platform() with preprocessor.

   Upstream guards these calls with MP_HAS() and relies on compiler to
   eliminate calls to functions not defined for target platform. Clang does
   not do this without optimization, which makes linking fail (upstream's
   CMake build works around this by forcing -O1).

2) Fill entire buffer in s_read_urandom() when read() returns less than
   requested.

   Read loop always reads into beginning of buffer, leaving rest of it
   without random data. This is a backport of upstream commit 528fdb0
   (s_mp_rand_platform.c: s_read_urandom: correctly handle split read),
   which is not yet in a release.

libtommath/bn_mp_set_double.c:

3) Compile mp_set_double() on all architectures with IEEE 754 doubles.

   Upstream only compiles this function if compiler defines __STDC_IEC_559__
   or __GCC_IEC_559, which MSVC and Clang on macOS and FreeBSD do not. On
   such platforms <tommath.h> declares mp_set_double() but library does not
   define it. This is a backport of upstream commit 4e90f31 (Build+test
   bn_mp_set_double.c on more platforms), which is not yet in a release.

Patches were made as follows (using bn_mp_set_double.c as example):

$ cd libtommath/
$ mv bn_mp_set_double.c bn_mp_set_double.c.orig
$ cp -H bn_mp_set_double.c.orig bn_mp_set_double.c
$ edit bn_mp_set_double.c
$ diff -u bn_mp_set_double.c.orig bn_mp_set_double.c >bn_mp_set_double.c.patch

To re-apply them after upgrading upstream submodule:

$ cd libtommath/
$ cp -H bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.orig bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c
$ patch <bn_s_mp_rand_platform.c.patch
$ cp -H bn_mp_set_double.c.orig bn_mp_set_double.c
$ patch <bn_mp_set_double.c.patch

Upstream dropped bn_ prefix from these file names on its develop branch,
where patches 2 and 3 are already applied and patch 1 is still required.
